---
title: Grown Up Ham and Cheese Finger Sandwiches
servings: 6
prepTime: 30 min
cookTime: 10 min
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 10/10
Description: "Do ahead tips: Toast the bread ahead, and thinly slice the apple, placing them in lemon water to prevent them from turning brown. If you need to assemble the sandwiches ahead, don't add the watercress, and cover them with a very light moistened paper towel."
source: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/grown-up-ham-and-cheese-finger-sandwiches-recipe-1928347
tags: Appetizer, Pork
---

= Onions =
Bring @water{1/2%cup}, @cider vinegar{3%tbsp}, and @brown sugar{1 1/2%tbsp} to a boil.
Add the @red onion{1/2}(very thinly sliced) and remove from the heat.
Cover, and set aside until the onions come to room temperature.

= Toast =
Preheat the oven to 400°F.

Trim the crusts off the @thin white bread{8%slices} and cut the bread into thirds, for 3 rectangles per piece.
Lightly brush both sides of the bread pieces with @Extra-virgin olive oil{} and lay out on a #baking sheet{}.
Toast in the oven until just crisp and lightly brown, about ~{5%minutes}. Cool.

= Assembly =
Quarter, core, and very thinly slice the @green apples{2}(small), (a mandolin is terrific for this).
Very thinly slice the @aged Gouda{6%oz} into triangles or shards that will fit nicely on the bread.

Place a dab or smear of @Dijon mustard{1%tbsp}(or whole grain mustard, apple butter or chutney) on the bread.
Place a piece of apple, cheese and 1 or 2 sprigs of @watercress{1/2%bunch} on each piece of toasted bread.

Wrap a small piece of @prosciutto{8%slices} around each stack to make a neat package.
Top with a little bit of the pickled onions, a drizzle of olive oil and freshly cracked @black pepper{}.
Serve at room temperature.

